    "plan": "This cycle: take a small exploratory position in NOVA (tiny size, similar to my usual $150-200 rotation amounts) — enough to participate if it pumps, small enough that a rug doesn't hurt my portfolio meaningfully. Set a mental stop: if NOVA drops significantly or GoldenWhale shows any exit signs, cut immediately. Continue rest of rotation lightly in SOL/BTC/ETH for continuity. Next cycle: reassess based on how NOVA behaves — if it's pumping and GoldenWhale hasn't dumped, consider adding; if it stalls or reverses, exit fast."
